'' RUN: READ into a ustring -- a variable, an array element, a field. fb_DataReadStr was
'' given the ustring itself and wrote narrow bytes into its UTF-16 buffer: "hello" printed
'' three unrelated characters, different on each run (fbc-examples repro run02). Now a
'' narrow temporary, then fb_UStrAssignFromA, as LINE INPUT does.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/read-ustring.bas -o tests/codegen/readustring.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/readustring.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/readustring.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: hello|world|elem|field| 5 4
